# SURVIVAL ARM (user 2026-11-13: "ok but stop and resume"). The arrival-stop policy, resumed from its
# step_1300000, with v52's LANE-CENTRE POTENTIAL SHAPING back ON -- the one reward term that prices
# being off-centre BEFORE the line is crossed.
#
# WHY. At 1.25M this arm scores 49/80 under the slow-arrival rule (Town01 27/40 vs wrong 1, Town05
# 22/40 vs 2, both p<1e-4) but drives only 34-66 m between fault ends, against c0's 325-886 m on the
# same cells, and on the episodes it loses it leaves the lane within 12-19 m (median path of a
# faulting episode; c0's is 68-249 m). Lane crossings are 9 of 13 and 15 of 17 of its faults, and
# junctions are NOT over-represented (12-31% of faults, c0 25%). It drives on c0's FROZEN trunk, so
# the features are sufficient -- the same features keep c0 in its lane 5-20x longer. What is missing
# is a signal the critic can attribute to a steering action: its Q is ~ V(s) + g(a)
# ([[critic-never-learns-steering-magnitude]]), so "this steering will cross a line in ten steps" is
# not learnable from the terminal fine alone.
#
# v52_reward.env ships LANE_CENTRE_K=2.0 LANE_HEADING_K=1.0 for exactly this failure ("in training a
# crossing never ended an episode, and nothing pointed at the centre, only the line"); the learner-C
# overlay chain inherits slurm/sac_scratch_*, which zeroes both -- the running job prints
# "c = 0 where the body meets the line + 0 at 45 deg heading error".
#
# POTENTIAL-BASED, so it is not a difficulty knob: F = c(s) - gamma c(s'), c = 0 at a terminal state,
# the discounted sum telescopes to c(start), and no early end can ever be made cheaper (Ng, Harada &
# Russell 1999). It cannot change the optimal policy; it moves the information one step closer to the
# action. The crossing fine still prices crossings.
#
# REWARD-ONLY PRIVILEGED INFO: core_state.LANE_GEOM turns on automatically when either K > 0 and
# publishes info["lane_priv"] from the CARLA map; the DEBiT observation never reads it, so the
# navigator stays image-only. To be DISCLOSED in the paper beside the expert's action labels.
#
# ONE CHANGE, deliberately: the steer-change cost (LF_K_STEER_CHANGE) stays off, so that any movement
# in metres-per-fault is attributable to the shaping. It is the next thing to try if this does nothing.
#
# DECLARED GATE, written before the first result: at step 1,325,000 (resume + 25k) metres per fault
# end must be >= 150 (it is 34-66 now; c0 is 325-886) AND strict goal SR must not fall below 30/80.
# Otherwise stop and report. Metric: scripts/paired_wrong.py for SR, and path_m / fault ends from
# eval.json (job tmp failure_rate.py).
#
# Everything else is the running arm's, unchanged: 4 towns stepped in parallel on 2 L40s, batched
# critic heads, pinned expert replay, GOAL_ARRIVAL_MAX_SPEED=10, 2M total budget (user: "the step
# budget is 2M").
. "$REPO/slurm/cluster_frl_c0emb_4towns_arrivalstop_pilot.env"
export LANE_CENTRE_K=2.0 LANE_HEADING_K=1.0
export FRL_RESUME=$HOME/carla-rl/checkpoints/frl_c0emb_4towns_arrivalstop/step_1300000
export FRL_MAX_STEPS=2000000
